nc_to_project":"","file_format":"png","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","wrap_mode":"limited","pbr_channel":"color","fps":7,"frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":false,"uuid":"9d4069b4-dd5a-f7d5-0bf2-c4e699bd0652","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"description":"## witchwood\n\nMaterial, witchwood (Patch 7).\n\n- Cubes: 9 (3 rotated). Texture 32x32, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -8.0..8.5, y -3.0..1.1, z -7.0..-1.3 (size 16.5 x 4.1 x 5.7 u = 46 x 12 x 16 cm).\nWitchwood: the dark, gnarled staff wood left over when casters' staffs are scrapped. Three crooked lengths of dark wood with a faint violet sheen on their tops (each bent once at a knot), tied together with two cords, in the style of `bone_bundle`. Origin = **slot_carry** (front of the chest), as `bone_bundle`: the load sits in both arms, its back face at about z = 0 against the chest. To stand it on the ground as a pile/prop, place the origin at y = 3.0. Patch 7.\n"}